  <component name="VcsManagerConfiguration">
    <MESSAGE value="#355:When write to Wav LIST fields need to write as IS0-8859-1 not UTF-8" />
    <MESSAGE value="#655:Issue writing to Wav file because INFO chunk has invalid field and this prevents reading of subsequent data chunk" />
    <MESSAGE value="#656:Add support for CREDITS,URL_BANDCAMP_ARTIST_SITE and URL_BANDCAMP_RELEASE_SITE" />
    <MESSAGE value="#658:For Wav Files allow to read Riff Files using a different encoding to the official ISO-8859-1 encoding" />
    <MESSAGE value="#659:For files that have ID3 tag allow for frames with text encoding set to zero (ISO-8859-1) allow to read as different encoding instead" />
    <MESSAGE value="Only use override charset for fields listed in TagOptionSingleton.getInstance().getOverrideCharset()" />
    <MESSAGE value="Modify ID3 tags so now take note of the overrideCharset field list, and only does override if field is in list.&#10;Also, overrideCharset has no effect on some text fields. If the text field is a description field to further subdivide a frame into versions for different data (most notably FrameBodyTXXX and FrameBodyCOMM description fields) we use the standard encoding when reading the metadata because software would usually only write   wrong charset into the value field not the description field." />
    <MESSAGE value="#622:Add ENGINEER subtypes AUDIO_ENGINEER, BALANCE_ENGINEER, AUDIO_ENGINEER, SOUND_ENGINEER and also MASTERING plus sort fields" />
    <MESSAGE value="Fix Mastering incorrectly mapped to unsymc lyrics" />
    <MESSAGE value="#663:Handle m4a without an audio info (esds or alac) atom" />
    <MESSAGE value="#665:For Mp4 support disk atom that uses type of text (0x01) rather than type implict (0x00) (expects a number value )" />
    <MESSAGE value="Fixed some tests sometimes failing because we have multiple tests creating file with same name in testdatatmp causing race conditions, now ensure that files have unique name." />
    <MESSAGE value="Removed use of pattern matching instanceof code because we require code to be compatible with java 1.8&#10;Remoe replaygain fields added to FieldKey because dont have support for them in all tag formats so was breaking tests" />
    <MESSAGE value="Wavpack and Ape test Files and tests that currently fail on reading files" />
    <MESSAGE value="#667:Add support for ALBUM_COMPOSER" />
    <MESSAGE value="Fixed ape/wavpack test file names" />
    <MESSAGE value="#667:Also added ALBUM_COMPOSER_SORT" />
    <MESSAGE value="For VorbisComment MusicBRainz Album Type shpuld be mapped to RELEASETYPE" />
    <MESSAGE value="#263:Unable to read multiple genres in an m4a file when one genre is custom and one is standard" />
    <MESSAGE value="+ rewrite to kt" />
    <MESSAGE value="README: verified JitPack coordinates" />
    <MESSAGE value="Chunked FileChannel IO operations and updated Android openFileIo implementation&#10;&#10;- Chunked `FileChannelIo` read and write calls in 64KB increments on JVM and Android to cap NIO direct memory allocations per thread.&#10;- Updated `openFileIo` on Android to create `FileChannel` via `RandomAccessFile` for better compatibility.&#10;- Added unit tests covering read, write, position, and EOF behavior in `FileChannelIoTest`.&#10;- Updated IDE project module configuration files for multiplatform target support." />
    <MESSAGE value="Upgraded Kotlin to 2.4.20 and improved ASF, MP4, and ID3v2 tag handling&#10;&#10;- Upgraded Kotlin version to 2.4.20 and Gradle wrapper to 8.14.5.&#10;- Implemented full ASF metadata container distribution supporting Content Description, Extended Content, Metadata, and Metadata Library objects.&#10;- Added `PartOfSet` frame handling for ID3v2 TRCK/TPOS and MP4 `trkn`/`disk` atoms to preserve track/disc numbers and totals.&#10;- Separated standard `gnre` uint16 genres and custom `©gen` text genres in MP4 tags.&#10;- Updated Vorbis `ALBUM_ARTIST` and ID3v2 comment/lyrics frame handling.&#10;- Added Java parity unit tests and test dependency against `jaudiotagger:3.0.1`." />
    <MESSAGE value="Fix ID3v2 zero-size frame parsing and improve MP3 duration calculations&#10;&#10;- Skip zero-size ID3v2 frames in `Id3v2TagReader` instead of terminating tag parsing.&#10;- Update `MpegFrameHeader` to use 576 samples per frame for MPEG-2/2.5 Layer III.&#10;- Improve frame count estimation in `Mp3InfoReader` when Xing/VBRI frame count is zero or missing by inspecting subsequent audio frames.&#10;- Add unit tests for empty ID3v2 frames and MP3 duration calculations, and update `PORTING.md`." />
    <MESSAGE value="kt scanner" />
    <option name="LAST_COMMIT_MESSAGE" value="kt scanner" />
  </component>
